      "writtenOn": "2024-08-09T22:34:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct - `ReadTraitAdapterForSkStream` doesn\u0027t own anything.  But (not in this CL, but in the follow-up) something needs to own `ReadTraitAdapterForSkStream` so that it\u0027s lifetime matches (or is longer than) the lifetime of `png::Reader` (which gets the `Read` trait object by value).\n\nMaybe I can just rewrite the comment to avoid talking about distant motivations and just say that the destructor supports passing `UniquePtr\u003cReadTrait\u003e` over the FFI boundary.  (Passing `UniquePtr\u003cReadTrait\u003e` over the FFI boundary already happens in *this* CL, even though we won\u0027t retain `UniquePtr` for longer time until the follow-up CL.)",
